abstract: >-
  Python framework for investigating organized mathematical objects under
  declared nodal laws. It treats the thirteen registered structural operators,
  their grammar and atomic execution stages as the constitutive mechanisms
  under study; continuous, native relational and collective descriptions must
  be grounded in actual operator execution or a proved realization. This
  release integrates operator-level results on maintenance and ordered return,
  synthesis, coupling, Emission, Mutation and recursive participation with
  shared kernels and tests, and resolves four foundation prerequisites within
  reviewed mathematical scopes; physical mapping remains gated behind a final
  readiness review. The research program is modular and the repository keeps
  the material that serves active questions; retired secondary evidence is
  linked to its recovery commit. Each release ships a lightweight development
  bundle. Exact identities, conditional proofs and finite computational
  evidence do not constitute empirical validation or select a unique
  fundamental law.
